    "duck": "Estimated from saved music/background-audio volume and duck-gain envelopes; source dynamics are unknown. Unavailable if no bed or speech/gap windows exist.",
    "frame": "108x192 grey affine-photometric MAD +/-3 source frames (best/second cost ratio <=0.9 and absolute separation >=0.02) with float perspective alignment; no integer crop approximation. EDL cuts are excluded. Text envelopes are masked on both source and output; unknown animated geometry is unmeasured. Expected indices use the global grid, source rate and speed, clamped to exact ffprobe nb_frames when available. Intended EOF/rate-conversion/slow-motion holds are not judder. Animated mappings and ambiguous static frames reduce coverage.",
    "camera": "Source-referenced small-translation least squares with affine brightness fit on 108x192 decoded grey frames; masked overlay envelopes and gradient neighbours. SG7 high-frequency residual normalized to 1080 short side. Flat/aperture/poor fits are unavailable; requires 95% eligible coverage. Physical source motion cancels against the same expected source frame. This estimate does not certify source-frame identity. The old whole-picture measure remains content_motion_jitter_px. Compare measurement version4 before and after only. Version4 corrects only the aggregate frame denominator from the original saved registration counts; the original version3 file is retained separately.",
    "delivery": "Format qualityChecks (excluding whole-content motion) plus ffprobe codec, BT.709 and audio bitrate; trace_headers verifies IDR keyframes and ffprobe timestamps verify CFR. Motion retains its separate source-referenced gates."
